<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Natwarsinhji Bhavsinhji</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a>–<a href="/years/1979">1979</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Maharaja of Porbandar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Natwarsinhji Bhavsinhji was the last ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Porbandar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a>, from 1908 until the state joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1948. A keen cricketer, he captained the Indian team on its tour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1932, the first by an official Indian side, although he stood down for the one Test match, in which C. K. Nayudu led India.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/natwarsinhji-bhavsinhji.jpg" alt="Natwarsinhji Bhavsinhji" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Natwarsinhji_Bhavsinhji_1932.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
